--TEST--
The four type names refusing what they do not hold: a `callable` given a function's name as text, a call through one used without converting it, a plain `string` at the two sites that take a class reference, and a shape literal short of a field it names (`rule:types/callable-values`, `rule:types/class-reference-sites`, `rule:types/shape-type`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:types/callable-classes-object-shapes

class Cell {
    public int $n = 1;
    public static function make(): string {
        return "made";
    }
}

// `rule:types/callable-values`: a closure is the only thing a
// `callable` holds, so there is no callable string to fall back on.
callable $named = "strtoupper";

// `rule:types/callable-values`: a call through a `callable` value
// answers `mixed`, which does not widen into anything narrower on its own.
callable $double = fn(int $x): int => $x * 2;
int $four = $double(2);

// `rule:types/class-reference-sites`: a class's name as text is not a class
// reference, and the sites that take one refuse a bare `string` rather than
// resolving a name at run time.
string $name = "Cell";
echo $name::make(), "\n";
object $o = new Cell();
echo ($o is $name) ? "y" : "n", "\n";

// `rule:types/shape-type`: a shape is satisfied by the fields a value
// carries, so a literal missing one it names does not satisfy it.
type Point = {x: int, y: int};
Point $short = {x: 1};
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0418]: a string is not callable in Novis. Use a method reference instead
%A
error[E0401]: expected `int`, found `mixed`
%A
error[E0496]: the class side of a `::` call must be a written class name
%A
error[E0496]: the right-hand side of `is` is a type or a class reference, and this is neither
%A
error[E0401]: expected `{x: int, y: int}`, found `{x: int}`
%A
error: aborting due to 5 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
